\subsection{Manipulation control across benchmarks}
\label{sec:exp-manipulation}

\aditya{Update Goal-conditioned \name{} numbers}
We next evaluate \name{} on 11 manipulation tasks from OGBench, MetaWorld, and ManiSkill, and locomotion tasks in DMC (\cref{tab:benchmarks}).
Dataset details are provided in \cref{app:data-mw-ms}.
\name{} achieves higher mean success than FB on every task, with average gains of $35.5$, $43.6$, and $29.7$ percentage points on OGBench, MetaWorld, and ManiSkill, respectively.
It also exceeds HILP and RLDP on all 11 tasks.

Against the goal-conditioned baselines, \name{} achieves the highest mean success on seven tasks, including all five ManiSkill tasks.
GCIQL performs better on \texttt{cube-double}, while QRL has higher mean success on the three MetaWorld tasks.
For \name{}, each downstream task is specified through rewards on $10^4$ offline states, which are used to infer a task vector without further training.

